{"h":3106,"w":2400,"lines":[{"t":"Reading","x":0.78660690940740019,"y":0.064309343272214714,"h":0.020494184721230102,"c":1,"w":0.079087193806966161},{"w":0.73120300292968743,"h":0.017498951609182356,"c":1,"y":0.11482558126339937,"x":0.063909776629288706,"t":"importance in a quite different sphere, as Alfred Nobel introduced the world to his"},{"t":"nitroglycerine-based invention: dynamite.","x":0.06578947300212766,"y":0.13361236290429446,"h":0.017707662588538398,"w":0.37969924926757809,"c":1},{"y":0.16999356097606122,"t":"Their biology would appear to make coconuts the great maritime voyagers and coastal","w":0.78007517496744794,"h":0.017506439150032249,"c":1,"x":0.06578948008595091},{"w":0.77631576538085945,"x":0.065789485651771146,"h":0.01744186072217524,"c":1,"y":0.18895348824110003,"t":"colonizers of the plant world. The large, energy-rich fruits are able to float in water and"},{"t":"tolerate salt, but cannot remain viable indefinitely; studies suggest after about 110 days","y":0.2078488370785424,"w":0.78571426391601562,"c":1,"x":0.063909785239076963,"h":0.017521414231732035},{"t":"at sea they are no longer able to germinate. Literally cast onto desert island shores,","x":0.065741506843697367,"y":0.22517796367307552,"w":0.75387186686197916,"h":0.019033142772706513,"c":1},{"w":0.75765996297200511,"x":0.06384859611359768,"y":0.2418137861766434,"t":"with little more than sand to grow in and exposed to the full glare of the tropical sun,","h":0.021300979683035459,"c":1},{"c":1,"x":0.065708813546624084,"w":0.79528101603190104,"t":"coconut seeds are able to germinate and root. The air pocket in the seed, created as the","y":0.25994991308781501,"h":0.022528845497814198},{"w":0.77631576538085934,"c":1,"h":0.017443732453866434,"x":0.065789485639222586,"t":"endosperm solidifies, protects the embryo. In addition, the fibrous fruit wall that helped","y":0.28197674405533679},{"c":1,"x":0.063909774340662959,"h":0.017543876240196599,"y":0.30087209289249595,"t":"it to float during the voyage stores moisture that can be taken up by the roots of the","w":0.75},{"x":0.063909769549784792,"t":"coconut seedling as it starts to grow.","w":0.33082707722981775,"c":1,"h":0.016097875080489321,"y":0.31970379901860935},{"c":1,"h":0.016097875080489432,"x":0.06390977204395408,"y":0.35608499647848357,"t":"There have been centuries of academic debate over the origins of the coconut. There","w":0.76879699707031246},{"c":1,"h":0.021281299480529148,"x":0.063837181269553109,"y":0.37258972374896859,"w":0.78209752400716148,"t":"were no coconut palms in West Africa, the Caribbean or the east coast of the Americas"},{"w":0.75751881917317709,"h":0.017441860722175129,"c":1,"x":0.063909763048906526,"y":0.39244186032931938,"t":"before the voyages of the European explorers Vasco da Gama and Columbus in the"},{"y":0.41120319532866845,"t":"late 15th and early 16th centuries. 16th century trade and human migration patterns","w":0.75386082967122392,"h":0.018903665978603046,"c":1,"x":0.063856836218813648},{"w":0.77255640665690106,"c":1,"h":0.017539196296883608,"x":0.062030067205400691,"t":"reveal that Arab traders and European sailors are likely to have moved coconuts from","y":0.43013522243245528},{"c":1,"h":0.016141863845658078,"y":0.44752092712039548,"t":"South and Southeast Asia to Africa and then across the Atlantic to the east coast of","x":0.063909774298593708,"w":0.75},{"x":0.063853343482219702,"c":1,"h":0.018769455201688712,"y":0.46645203889906262,"t":"America. But the origin of coconuts discovered along the west coast of America by","w":0.74071039835611974},{"x":0.063909766497033713,"h":0.01744186072217524,"c":1,"t":"16th century sailors has been the subject of centuries of discussion. Two diametrically","w":0.77255640665690106,"y":0.4854651161482868},{"h":0.018895348808647183,"t":"opposed origins have been proposed: that they came from Asia, or that they were native","w":0.79323308308919271,"x":0.063909766820065481,"y":0.5014534881501822,"c":1},{"t":"to America. Both suggestions have problems. In Asia, there is a large degree of coconut","x":0.063909774109837558,"h":0.018895348808647183,"c":1,"w":0.79323308308919271,"y":0.52180232559226569},{"y":0.54056664508636576,"c":1,"h":0.017707662588538287,"w":0.76315790812174478,"t":"diversity and evidence of millennia of human use - but there are no relatives growing","x":0.063909767647501586},{"c":1,"t":"in the wild. In America, there are close coconut relatives, but no evidence that coconuts","y":0.55956213770931118,"h":0.017472746137335293,"x":0.065789464577146073,"w":0.78195490519205735},{"t":"are indigenous. These problems have led to the intriguing suggestion that coconuts","y":0.57848837196159653,"x":0.063909774322121679,"w":0.75,"c":1,"h":0.017454963458098605},{"y":0.59593023242438792,"h":0.01744186072217524,"c":1,"x":0.063909786881678254,"t":"originated on coral islands in the Pacific and were dispersed from there.","w":0.64661651611328119},{"y":0.97529069768122989,"t":"61","x":0.82894736804622371,"w":0.02443609078725173,"h":0.013081395234588844,"c":1}]}